INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - FIRE DRILL - DAY

A chandeliered room set for a banquet no one will attend. Round tables, white cloths, a podium. An alarm klaxon whoops overhead.

BARCLAY PENHALLOW-DIOP (50s, regional director, bluetooth earpiece) stands on a chair waving a laminated evacuation map. ROSAMUND TAKAHASHI-FINN (30s, safety warden, high-vis vest over a pantsuit) points a megaphone at the exits. WINSTON ABERNATHY-KOH (60s, accountant, gripping his briefcase) sits calmly at a table, peeling an orange.

BARCLAY
Everybody remain calm and form an orderly line!

ROSAMUND
(through the megaphone)
Sir, please step down from the chair.

BARCLAY
I'm elevated for visibility!

ROSAMUND
You're elevated for liability!

Winston peels a long ribbon of orange. Barclay jumps down, stumbles, and knocks over a centerpiece. Rosamund rushes to catch it, collides with Barclay, and both go down in a heap of tablecloth and carnations. The klaxon whoops. Winston places an orange segment in his mouth.

WINSTON
Is it a real fire?

ROSAMUND
(muffled, from the floor)
It's a drill!

WINSTON
Then why are you on the floor?

BARCLAY
(also from the floor)
Realism.

The klaxon cuts off. Silence settles over the ballroom like a bad dream. Winston finishes the orange. Rosamund and Barclay untangle slowly. Barclay straightens his earpiece.

BARCLAY (CONT'D)
Good. Excellent. Very instructive.

ROSAMUND
Sir, you failed.

BARCLAY
I failed instructively.
